#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157123 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157319 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "947c8ce4-53c5-5765-ab74-62daf58e53e1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Graph Transformations Resulting From Reflections With Shifting"}] :question/id #uuid "437933c3-8c8b-52b8-84f0-ea6bbf789552" :question/math-academy-id "e-7516" :question/problem "The diagram below shows the function $y=f(x).$ Find the graph of $y=-f(x+3).$\n\n![](images/8c/8c57e0ebec3c6dcc4b6d1b72a8dde395fbe4a90801c18718fc36edf84469af4f.png)" :question/worked-solution "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches and reflections, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches and reflections, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo plot $y=-f(x+3),$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Translate it to the left by $3$ units $y=f(x+3).$\n\n![](images/07/0770e092f1d63c0a9c4416f92fa6e543ffcc47bcd78375f5b835b64df3ef691a.png)\n\n- Then, reflect the result across the  $x$- axis to get the graph of $y=-f(x+3).$\n\n![](images/5f/5fde1d3543593322ad5caebbf28d4623571032e35c516dd051583294f452e679.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157198 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157378 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff702318-379a-5040-b32f-e7c89f1f2451" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Correct Order of Transformations Given a Transformed Function Expression"}] :question/id #uuid "e2417b4a-ffe8-5dc3-946e-d4c7e9a09719" :question/math-academy-id "e-8653" :question/problem "The graph of $y=-f(x-2)+3,$ can be obtained from the graph of $y=f(x)$ by applying **some** of the following transformations:\n\n- $(\\textrm{T}1)$ - Translation by $3$ units up\n\n- $(\\textrm{T}2)$ - Reflection across the $x$-axis\n\n- $(\\textrm{T}3)$ - Translation by $2$ units to the right\n\n- $(\\textrm{T}4)$ - Translation by $2$ units to the left\n\nWhat could be a possible ordering of the appropriate transformations?" :question/worked-solution "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches and reflections, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches and reflections, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo get $y=-f(x-2)+3,$ we could apply the following steps: \n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Apply transformation $(\\textrm{T}3)\\mathbin{:}$ Translate $y=f(x)$ by $2$ units to the right to get the graph of \n\n$$\ny=f(x-2).\n$$\n\n- Apply transformation $(\\textrm{T}2)\\mathbin{:}$ Reflect $y=f(x-2)$ across the $x$-axis to get the graph of \n\n$$\ny=-f(x-2).\n$$\n\n- Apply transformation $(\\textrm{T}1)\\mathbin{:}$ Translate $y=-f(x-2)$ by $3$ units up to get the graph of \n\n$$\ny=-f(x-2)+3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, a possible order of transformations is\n\n$\\qquad$ $(\\textrm{T}3) \\to (\\textrm{T}2) \\to (\\textrm{T}1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157199 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157379 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0bf39b4-5615-5078-b048-99bbd7c50b50" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Graph Transformations Resulting From Reflections With Scaling"}] :question/id #uuid "86213aa7-5452-547b-9a8d-467bf870bc08" :question/math-academy-id "e-8654" :question/problem "The diagram below shows the function $y=f(x).$ Find the graph of $y=f\\left(-3x\\right).$\n\n![](images/7a/7a0aac61b989b6aac26352c2f3faa05fc87ef37ec8ec9e120c83eabd213ed245.png)" :question/worked-solution "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches and reflections, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches and reflections, followed by vertical translations.\n\nFirst, let's factor out the minus sign next to the $x$ inside the function:\n\n$$\ny=f\\left(-\\left(3x\\right)\\right)\n$$\n\nTo plot $y=f\\left(-\\left(3x\\right)\\right),$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Stretch it by a scale factor of $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ parallel to the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=f\\left(3x\\right).$\n\n![](images/c8/c858bf111c2dbc55aa3308276d5ee93aaa0f7a0b4e5b4b69e749f552bd548d57.png)\n\n- Then, reflect it across the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=f\\left(-\\left(3x\\right)\\right).$\n\n![](images/25/25bcd904d279c4e054e5d66b731ef294a3c1441d28e916c2824f99b9f16a3b7e.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157200 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157380 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4529c46f-0656-523f-a403-65477ea040f2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Graph Transformations Resulting From Reflections With Other Transformations"}] :question/id #uuid "3b032f9c-3c15-5018-ae45-28b01235a3c7" :question/math-academy-id "e-8655" :question/problem "The diagram below shows the function $y=f(x).$ Find the graph of $y=3f\\left(-x+1\\right)?$\n\n![](images/ca/ca4445101ef048b82262dcca5a91d249bcf1c3172417def297ddd45cb59b9053.png)" :question/worked-solution "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches and reflections, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches and reflections, followed by vertical translations.\n\nFirst, let's factor out the negative sign next to the $x$ inside the function:\n\n$$\ny=3f\\left(-(x-1)\\right)\n$$\n\nTo plot $y=3f\\left(-(x-1)\\right),$ we apply the following steps: \n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Reflect it across the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=f\\left(-x\\right)$ (remember that multiplication comes *before* subtraction in the order of operations).\n\n![](images/6c/6cde0cf55bd7a80cfb717eac89288dc99cede1b8456a0140d3e30c741958793d.png)\n\n \n\n- Then, translate the result by $1$ unit to the right to get the graph of $y=f\\left(-(x-1)\\right).$\n\n![](images/80/803eb49b759eb31716470db93878fd2f3b73aaa0d8085bacd4be5a5f6706254d.png)\n\n- Finally, stretch the result by a scale factor of $3$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=3f\\left(-(x-1)\\right).$\n\n![](images/37/3781afe1b28d36c73f2831461fee136d93a6bfe4439f47bb96dfb462a62677e2.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554643 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157379 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0bf39b4-5615-5078-b048-99bbd7c50b50" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Graph Transformations Resulting From Reflections With Scaling"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06c9dab7-2e99-5365-b6f9-2f92a770a384" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0e/0e49310e5441552232d841954e95fe3b38015b27565050fbd384d54b35a56bfc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553883} {:answer/id #uuid "11d75bbb-77b6-5e55-baef-b5f3c412881a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8f/8f8f679798bf48d8543522dfc3c77c25de4ebfd55618c17ea033549caea2f40a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553906} {:answer/id #uuid "56a351e4-0067-508f-9e5a-e7e8908908cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3d/3d4a416592d9fe3683f6b39bb99ebef44d3f0b36c37b50f86c9dac5fa8aa862f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554038} {:answer/id #uuid "89c6681c-3b74-5712-ac28-f5586469ed52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d2/d2dad7c3e898a680e07eba09d822733619f1158f9877136ba11078e90cbf75c2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554159} {:answer/id #uuid "e204c221-f408-5b2f-b387-49819b320673" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/eb/eb85e0857a24ae273e7e768c51e80c08461be095e502e45c2c83e7340bf725b2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06c9dab7-2e99-5365-b6f9-2f92a770a384" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0e/0e49310e5441552232d841954e95fe3b38015b27565050fbd384d54b35a56bfc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553883} :answer-field/id #uuid "16b058af-5b74-55ea-8310-41c6fb4502e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554441}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f73ff2c0-b98a-5833-8e43-d855656798f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-114069" :question/problem "![](images/93/938babc27340209a1a5477fb3184abbf155f409c520c76995c4e234f99691347.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the function $y=f(x).$ Which of the following gives the graph of $y=-f(\\frac{x}{3})?$" :question/worked-solution "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches and reflections, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches and reflections, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo plot $y=-f(\\frac{x}{3}),$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Stretch it by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{(\\frac{1}{3})}=3$ parallel to the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=f(\\frac{x}{3}).$\n\n![](images/f0/f0b289d42620a275eeb90d4bdbe265ca92ea4264de70ecc11e5f661a84149628.png)\n\n- Then, reflect the result across the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=-f(\\frac{x}{3}).$\n\n![](images/59/597ba19a0c993ea597ecd091df02d97e974364125c79780df04aef365442abb6.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554624 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157380 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4529c46f-0656-523f-a403-65477ea040f2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Graph Transformations Resulting From Reflections With Other Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3abf1eb5-d7e3-5fa0-8c42-70389de225ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8b/8b612ba10fddfa21f2d4495aa24adbe05fcb66b14fc682c78b163608e2d5a947.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553975} {:answer/id #uuid "50297d59-a216-5c1c-9ae6-f8e0b94604a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8f/8fdd077596cc508337947993d13bf197900e30d2ea21e54efce259a45036a127.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554024} {:answer/id #uuid "867b22c8-ce8f-5bf6-ab0a-c1c5ac398bdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/27/27e807f3030f8780b64f7b80ce2da692d5a846da112c30215cefd13bd84a5fbd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554148} {:answer/id #uuid "9a53deaf-916f-500d-9688-841cfd82731d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c8/c8017c06848a7f9749742c28fed944a03fb4a6a46e2dc02e029a79d55fa20d50.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554205} {:answer/id #uuid "a5dc6a84-b562-5e83-845a-a691eafb3f4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fd/fde3bcc2394f7630ca77f137a3e7f8a2afa3b75d10a11e6f50beaa74da197719.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554234}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "867b22c8-ce8f-5bf6-ab0a-c1c5ac398bdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/27/27e807f3030f8780b64f7b80ce2da692d5a846da112c30215cefd13bd84a5fbd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554148} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4af18f8-8206-55c1-b168-26e7b4b9d10e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554525}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d8c07848-a1dd-5eb7-8320-0b4777fcd645" :question/math-academy-id "q-115013" :question/problem "![](images/85/8536196127d1e8fc92cd2d442005a386b2d981a027a497ecce363559f52ac0e6.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the function $y=f(x).$ Which of the following gives the graph of $y=-\\frac{5}{2}f(x)-4?$" :question/worked-solution "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches and reflections, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches and reflections, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo plot $y=-\\frac{5}{2}f(x)-4,$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Stretch it by a scale factor of $\\frac{5}{2}$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=\\frac{5}{2}f(x).$\n\n![](images/ba/bafacd18cae6114ad22fb59d905a8ebb68cc8768a5b20a4a5a2e36f59c11ad11.png)\n\n- Then, reflect the result across the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\frac{5}{2}f(x).$\n\n![](images/bd/bd69db18de3d58e6806b7ee3473a0fd4e8b6df384cf371be4e9648cac53e3927.png)\n\n- Finally, translate the result down by $4$ units to get the graph of $y=-\\frac{5}{2}f(x)-4.$\n\n![](images/fe/fe2e7245978e120a538cc87a31d6180c4e342fc438240be1f3ce367eed64bb33.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554557 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157380 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4529c46f-0656-523f-a403-65477ea040f2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Graph Transformations Resulting From Reflections With Other Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c61c420-b613-5fa5-9767-aa23853b7af8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2d/2d8a417e4b26d0683eda81d753f68a5d98ec42f4c7963490a0a3d3948a3c9d3d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553979} {:answer/id #uuid "65fec13d-35d9-52cc-a4e8-f31af1e88cfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fb/fb61bbc5809f3164d23db34848e8d634807489dd48f17f81ba7311ac24ee19fe.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554070} {:answer/id #uuid "b8d290dd-50f1-5bb7-9b1b-db031ef83878" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/49/49a77258ee0af7b356079e9f233ddb9bf81a77442e01c1a677b4ac442a2440d0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554271} {:answer/id #uuid "be653d9c-7610-5fa4-ae30-fe00750e5ab8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ae/aecf2160494e12ae8a73bcef802aeec9c61d59f59d81ab9533cbda9edcfc8b44.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554283} {:answer/id #uuid "f9bd2436-35ce-568b-8676-99947a0269b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/69/698ed28a31a3f81ab1fa8d7a8eb017dba9ecc2c4e2d677bb74ec4d98888745a2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554408}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c61c420-b613-5fa5-9767-aa23853b7af8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2d/2d8a417e4b26d0683eda81d753f68a5d98ec42f4c7963490a0a3d3948a3c9d3d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553979} :answer-field/id #uuid "aeba0eb8-45b2-596a-a008-a7c9b43c3677" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554497}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2b3b851a-20c6-5158-b86d-a090b5acc8fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-115018" :question/problem "![](images/5b/5b3e36d9b39fcc8d61fe30219d2f3191a1b305a44995b27d5daddb5f18926e02.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the function $y=f(x).$ Which of the following gives the graph of $y=-f(x-2)-4?$" :question/worked-solution "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches and reflections, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches and reflections, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo plot $y=-f(x-2)-4,$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Translate it by $2$ units to the right to get the graph of $y=f(x-2).$\n\n![](images/48/482f1dc55995a299b21894c0ec191c0f8fb8213038cdc5f80da1e77a0d64af4e.png)\n\n- Then, reflect the result across the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=-f(x-2).$\n\n![](images/a2/a2832ebdf82e2a7bfddccf24fd598758e1ce86fc0726f9c128503574b09fcd0b.png)\n\n- Finally, translate it down by $4$ units to get the graph of $y=-f(x-2)-4.$\n\n![](images/94/9473b7ebfbe7db3d1cfefcf3f7b616ffec4b9ad2e685a6fc40f4560e8d2a1c59.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554607 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157380 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4529c46f-0656-523f-a403-65477ea040f2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Graph Transformations Resulting From Reflections With Other Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67bc3dc8-9412-57da-b948-67be931cf23a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9e/9e29de3350d7e1729f7bbbc0345c4f0518df1b07ace92f36c1b0db43a5b985cf.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554074} {:answer/id #uuid "6f45ad7b-d454-5e2f-9ace-ce03f717e36a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/63/63e01f1062569e629b6dc8b004955db30ea97bfa9cc15025e17058300a628476.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554090} {:answer/id #uuid "9b1301d0-c9d3-524f-8d75-13c421d1d33f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e5/e52c421785b646c83ea29542a02e05c5f460ae8dab3b4e97d8148fe84704063a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554208} {:answer/id #uuid "c5832434-80d0-5574-9b32-b29a52fac560" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3e/3e2f9759b525575f97ee3c4a8d5684872e447edaa411c0fb5f605b50a9f553b8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554301} {:answer/id #uuid "fbba5cdd-b081-50bf-8bc3-7dfc2725fdab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/50/504024983dafee0fd49c0bb8227f33cc855e2ee9e4bb797f067f0a5e8e415815.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f45ad7b-d454-5e2f-9ace-ce03f717e36a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/63/63e01f1062569e629b6dc8b004955db30ea97bfa9cc15025e17058300a628476.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554090} :answer-field/id #uuid "790b63a4-2afd-58c9-a20f-656426972c93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554480}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "95bf6a06-ae4e-5d38-8c20-f91522b5fa5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-17696" :question/problem "![](images/50/504024983dafee0fd49c0bb8227f33cc855e2ee9e4bb797f067f0a5e8e415815.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the function $y=f(x).$ Which of the following gives the graph of $y=-4f(x-1)?$" :question/worked-solution "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches and reflections, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches and reflections, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo plot $y=-4f(x-1),$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Translate it by $1$ unit to the right to get the graph of $y=f(x-1).$\n\n![](images/d0/d07f918fae59166e137e47a2c654dfe77ce1c56bb71e931d2d627c509682823e.png)\n\n- Then, stretch the result by a scale factor of $4$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=4f(x-1).$\n\n![](images/4c/4c237eeb7ecb85ef71c86b73cdbeaae213e74a21604e079f0df4c14c381f6bd7.png)\n\n  \n\n- Finally, reflect the result across the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=-4f(x-1).$\n\n![](images/58/583f01b214d4c86dcb00936e83f1fad0a4f0f8901b321880d904b2f0da95d7e8.png)\n\n \n\n$$\n\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554553 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157380 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4529c46f-0656-523f-a403-65477ea040f2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Graph Transformations Resulting From Reflections With Other Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a6c53df-03c3-5272-b79f-e92b2df68cc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6b/6b4dec42ca9c8a54be8aa13f611907e5c7e3e4bce5e177c2cc5970bc2cf69735.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553974} {:answer/id #uuid "41d3f9e0-0839-5481-977d-ea32ab572300" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/88/88b831093808dba6820a2f8faeb3770ecf50f66ef56a0ef34887622eee639a30.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553989} {:answer/id #uuid "6f1cbf10-0914-558c-a35e-1b176c12da6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/83/839406ead3c7deda0ec0f783c01e1c99aca8877a7ba0ecfdb03f7adb883706fb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554089} {:answer/id #uuid "8901eefd-bfc8-5877-be0f-8a92a3ab82dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/17/175b02e0003de363b989f13f7ad4082ea6d87b56f8cc616605328ba775db5be2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554156} {:answer/id #uuid "db644941-4b47-5d57-9948-d42917f87daa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/58/587a9e679f9d446c8ae57ec93fadcb69ed423fd4803abd2150cd845ac1dc9558.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554348}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8901eefd-bfc8-5877-be0f-8a92a3ab82dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/17/175b02e0003de363b989f13f7ad4082ea6d87b56f8cc616605328ba775db5be2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554156} :answer-field/id #uuid "94669996-364b-5fcd-ac9d-e6a8be125a40" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554491}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "269fb630-a40e-5592-b4e3-251a076c8d27" :question/math-academy-id "q-17782" :question/problem "![](images/ef/efc577f386353b4120dec733e5e6a627ad2412744dce4d71deba2b500a1edec2.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the function $y=f(x).$ Which of the following gives the graph of $y=-f(\\frac{1}{2}x-1)?$" :question/worked-solution "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches and reflections, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches and reflections, followed by vertical translations.\n\nFirst, let's factor out the coefficient next to the $x$ inside the function:\n\n$$\ny=-f(\\frac{1}{2}(x-2))\n$$\n\nTo plot $y=-f(\\frac{1}{2}(x-2)),$ we apply the following steps: \n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Stretch it by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{(\\frac{1}{2})}=2$ parallel to the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=f(\\frac{1}{2}x).$\n\n![](images/28/2891d009bd6f5d026ca47afe90f3ec4d6fafc654b7212392b325f76fe43f806e.png)\n\n \n\n- Then, translate the result by $2$ units to the right to get the graph of $y=f(\\frac{1}{2}(x-2)).$\n\n![](images/ab/ab1f210741e01139618dc2fa1347cf1591cb90ca4f67906b89ebc7df29d77f32.png)\n\n- Finally, reflect the result across the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=-f(\\frac{1}{2}(x-2)).$\n\n![](images/e5/e5552a14dc62407e02bb8f5e633ae194a95d313bce04abb3186b56ce83ec2974.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157629 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157378 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff702318-379a-5040-b32f-e7c89f1f2451" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Correct Order of Transformations Given a Transformed Function Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "290e7843-220a-5a89-8fdb-575b887de178" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\text{T}3)\\to (\\text{T}2)\\to (\\text{T}4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553947} {:answer/id #uuid "58b4d56e-4ca9-5cda-b97d-7a3cf9baf086" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\text{T}4)\\to (\\text{T}3)\\to (\\text{T}2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554042} {:answer/id #uuid "5cef0025-ab5d-58b2-abc8-d28529eb5dd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\text{T}1)\\to (\\text{T}2)\\to (\\text{T}4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554050} {:answer/id #uuid "afd3f0e2-369a-516c-b862-b1b6ce58050e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\text{T}4)\\to (\\text{T}2)\\to (\\text{T}1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554258} {:answer/id #uuid "ec477bfb-f29c-5738-93e7-ba81e2c54bcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\text{T}4)\\to (\\text{T}1)\\to (\\text{T}2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554385}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afd3f0e2-369a-516c-b862-b1b6ce58050e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\text{T}4)\\to (\\text{T}2)\\to (\\text{T}1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554258} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fcf2f7f-47c9-5511-abd0-9f494a8dd82f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186154010}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4695eb04-f4a4-5bc8-8cb0-35703b6e89da" :question/math-academy-id "q-17848" :question/problem "The graph of $y=-f(2x)+4,$ can be obtained from the graph of $y=f(x)$ by applying **some** of the following transformations:\n\n- $(\\text{T}1)$ - Translation by $4$ units up\n\n- $(\\text{T}2)$ - Reflection across the $x$-axis\n\n- $(\\text{T}3)$ - Translation by $4$ units down\n\n- $(\\text{T}4)$ - Stretch of scale factor $\\frac{1}{2}$ parallel to the $x$-axis\n\nWhich of the following could be a possible ordering of the appropriate transformations?" :question/worked-solution "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches and reflections, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches and reflections, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo get $y=-f(2x)+4,$ we could apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Apply transformation $(\\text{T}4):$ Stretch $y=f(x)$ by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$ parallel to the $x$-axis to get the graph of \n\n$$\ny=f(2x).\n$$\n\n- Apply transformation $(\\text{T}2):$ Reflect $y=f(2x)$ across the $x$-axis to get the graph of \n\n$$\ny=-f(2x).\n$$\n\n- Apply transformation $(\\text{T}1):$ Translate $y=-f(2x)$ up by $4$ units to get the graph of \n\n$$\ny=-f(2x)+4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, a possible order of transformations is\n\n$\\,$ $(\\text{T}4)\\to (\\text{T}2)\\to (\\text{T}1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554611 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157378 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff702318-379a-5040-b32f-e7c89f1f2451" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Correct Order of Transformations Given a Transformed Function Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37bcc534-503f-59d4-9a82-79df30b5d695" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\text{T}4)\\to (\\text{T}3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553968} {:answer/id #uuid "551368a1-5a2b-53df-a888-581d3b746c74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\text{T}1)\\to (\\text{T}2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554032} {:answer/id #uuid "5573eca1-d3ad-5818-9703-94fc1488f674" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\text{T}2)\\to (\\text{T}3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554034} {:answer/id #uuid "83f8bd03-8875-57a2-9f70-253fd82cf18c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\text{T}1)\\to (\\text{T}3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554136} {:answer/id #uuid "8f97c969-cb30-5fff-a90b-aa56b316a079" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\text{T}4)\\to (\\text{T}2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554177}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f97c969-cb30-5fff-a90b-aa56b316a079" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\text{T}4)\\to (\\text{T}2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554177} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e9f64e3-d6b1-578a-a830-b151ec93c86a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554450}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a0d0470d-b24d-5636-b2cb-b9c005b7e95d" :question/math-academy-id "q-97783" :question/problem "The graph of $y=f(-(x+5))$ can be obtained from the graph of $y=f(x)$ by applying **some** of the following transformations:\n\n- $(\\text{T}1)$ - Reflection across the $x$-axis\n\n- $(\\text{T}2)$ - Translation by $5$ units to the left\n\n- $(\\text{T}3)$ - Stretch of scale factor $5$ parallel to the $y$-axis\n\n- $(\\text{T}4)$ - Reflection across the $y$-axis\n\nWhich of the following could be a possible ordering of the appropriate transformations?" :question/worked-solution "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches and reflections, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches and reflections, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo get $y=f(-(x+5)),$ we can apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Apply transformation $(\\text{T}4):$ Reflect $y=f(x)$ across the $y$-axis to get the graph of \n\n$$\ny=f(-x).\n$$\n\n- Apply transformation $(\\text{T}2):$ Translate $y=f(-x)$ to the left by $5$ units to get the graph of \n\n$$\ny=f(-(x+5)).\n$$\n\nTherefore, a possible order of transformations is\n\n$\\,$ $(\\text{T}4)\\to (\\text{T}2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554558 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157378 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff702318-379a-5040-b32f-e7c89f1f2451" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Correct Order of Transformations Given a Transformed Function Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26789c3a-4e14-5f12-8830-ad8e80298eff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\text{T}1)\\to (\\text{T}3)\\to (\\text{T}2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553940} {:answer/id #uuid "421e39a0-1464-5634-bd16-09b09f62a80d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\text{T}4)\\to (\\text{T}1)\\to (\\text{T}3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553990} {:answer/id #uuid "6f7f44c3-cb5a-5e0b-8947-661e68e70385" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\text{T}4)\\to (\\text{T}1)\\to (\\text{T}2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554093} {:answer/id #uuid "9d9505f9-71b5-5430-8d67-6cf06b21a0b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\text{T}4)\\to (\\text{T}3)\\to (\\text{T}1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554216} {:answer/id #uuid "a4d7a55f-1c9c-5f83-b9ef-bc5e8eb40426" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\text{T}4)\\to (\\text{T}3)\\to (\\text{T}2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554232}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4d7a55f-1c9c-5f83-b9ef-bc5e8eb40426" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\text{T}4)\\to (\\text{T}3)\\to (\\text{T}2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554232} :answer-field/id #uuid "0990bc9f-b980-589b-b932-ab04f3aca435" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554434}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2b4b8cea-e134-5e94-b33a-7dc117bff583" :question/math-academy-id "q-97785" :question/problem "The graph of $y=f(-2x)-1,$ can be obtained from the graph of $y=f(x)$ by applying **some** of the following transformations:\n\n- $(\\text{T}1)$ - Reflection across the $x$-axis\n\n- $(\\text{T}2)$ - Translation by $1$ unit down\n\n- $(\\text{T}3)$ - Reflection across the $y$-axis\n\n- $(\\text{T}4)$ - Stretch of scale factor $\\frac{1}{2}$ parallel to the $x$-axis\n\nWhich of the following could be a possible ordering of the appropriate transformations?" :question/worked-solution "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches and reflections, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches and reflections, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo get $y=f(-2x)-1,$ we could apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Apply transformation $(\\text{T}4):$ Stretch $y=f(x)$ by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$ parallel to the $x$-axis to get the graph of \n\n$$\ny=f(2x).\n$$\n\n- Apply transformation $(\\text{T}3):$ Reflect $y=f(2x)$ across the $y$-axis to get the graph of \n\n$$\ny=f(2(-x))=f(-2x).\n$$\n\n- Apply transformation $(\\text{T}2):$ Translate $y=f(-2x)$ down by $1$ unit to get the graph of \n\n$$\ny=f(-2x)-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, a possible order of transformations is\n\n$\\,$ $(\\text{T}4)\\to (\\text{T}3)\\to (\\text{T}2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554548 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157378 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff702318-379a-5040-b32f-e7c89f1f2451" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Correct Order of Transformations Given a Transformed Function Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09c17a4a-4f53-57c9-8f3c-4badcbcbacd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\text{T}3)\\to (\\text{T}4)\\to (\\text{T}2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553886} {:answer/id #uuid "3a37e768-dde7-5db7-8cba-08c9fe455725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\text{T}3)\\to (\\text{T}4)\\to (\\text{T}1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553973} {:answer/id #uuid "8edc4dd2-11b2-5482-9115-874fe418a3a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\text{T}1)\\to (\\text{T}4)\\to (\\text{T}2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554175} {:answer/id #uuid "a7e37100-4c73-555e-917a-6323823839b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\text{T}3)\\to (\\text{T}1)\\to (\\text{T}2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554241} {:answer/id #uuid "fdd525da-9b20-59fa-85be-c6ccda816d58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\text{T}4)\\to (\\text{T}3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554422}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09c17a4a-4f53-57c9-8f3c-4badcbcbacd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\text{T}3)\\to (\\text{T}4)\\to (\\text{T}2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553886} :answer-field/id #uuid "50c831bd-2f30-5cb8-8cf7-31fdc3d03f6f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554460}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1f3c3035-69e9-5d03-a0fc-4433cacd4260" :question/math-academy-id "q-97793" :question/problem "The graph of $y=-3f(4x),$ can be obtained from the graph of $y=f(x)$ by applying **some** of the following transformations:\n\n- $(\\text{T}1)$ - Reflection across the $y$-axis\n\n- $(\\text{T}2)$ - Reflection across the $x$-axis\n\n- $(\\text{T}3)$ - Stretch of scale factor $\\frac{1}{4}$ parallel to the $x$-axis\n\n- $(\\text{T}4)$ - Stretch of scale factor $3$ parallel to the $y$-axis\n\nWhich of the following could be a possible ordering of the appropriate transformations?" :question/worked-solution "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches and reflections, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches and reflections, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo get $y=-3f(4x),$ we could apply the following steps: \n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Apply transformation $(\\text{T}3):$ Stretch $y=f(x)$ by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{4}$ parallel to the $x$-axis to get the graph of \n\n$$\ny=f(4x).\n$$\n\n- Apply transformation $(\\text{T}4):$ Stretch $y=f(4x)$ by a scale factor of $3$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of \n\n$$\ny=3f(4x).\n$$\n\n- Apply transformation $(\\text{T}2):$ Reflect $y=3f(4x)$ across the $x$-axis to get the graph of \n\n$$\ny=-3f(4x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, a possible order of transformations is\n\n$\\,$ $(\\text{T}3)\\to (\\text{T}4)\\to (\\text{T}2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554580 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157379 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0bf39b4-5615-5078-b048-99bbd7c50b50" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Graph Transformations Resulting From Reflections With Scaling"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "029bdf82-6366-59d5-8cfa-a391eed8c109" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e7/e7a483986183ee2e4cbbc74af0432d5a43d6daeab23dd342830f6a31482a7599.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553870} {:answer/id #uuid "04e27a6e-92cf-578c-9e8a-3a5d5cbe0c3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/94/94ebe249199debf2f62fd62ff878d6a8e6207381dcf9474f48e28a35f3046278.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553877} {:answer/id #uuid "1b95e52b-0904-5971-bbc3-a4919450f05c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/39/39e8c399a890e3528289fa569c828d4f4ba27ebc08d52a279c24ca3f130414ed.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553920} {:answer/id #uuid "8fadb2c0-6442-5a83-af82-c9a725055c8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1b/1b691a987508ea114f1020a0d66b3c80558539a0a16ee7bf9f4fd6c0b77b5ed4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554178} {:answer/id #uuid "be5af0ba-9b31-5fec-8893-b738ec606742" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bd/bd7a0fb52338c43267c8e5be22e49796b4170ff83f0e184b09519ebbaeb67c21.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8fadb2c0-6442-5a83-af82-c9a725055c8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1b/1b691a987508ea114f1020a0d66b3c80558539a0a16ee7bf9f4fd6c0b77b5ed4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554178} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea82b50a-93b2-5cb1-8254-45300689e485" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554528}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "689e7bfc-91b5-5578-9523-c9029e296a11" :question/math-academy-id "q-97940" :question/problem "![](images/e5/e5138b92d20572b1680dfc010d6e0f8729de9c21c62448cdcb472efbf762c4d1.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the function $y=f(x).$ Which of the following gives the graph of $y=-f(-2x)?$" :question/worked-solution "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches and reflections, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches and reflections, followed by vertical translations.\n\nFirst, let's factor out the coefficient next to the $x$ inside the function:\n\n$$\ny=f(-(2x))\n$$\n\nTo plot $y=-f(-(2x)),$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Stretch it by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{2}$ parallel to the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=f(2x).$\n\n![](images/7d/7d76ce80b4212d0cb6cd8b64c424492dd46cad3819ce3cba17bab22c4df115f5.png)\n\n- Then, reflect the result across the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=f(-2x).$\n\n![](images/de/ded37839584d99725ab44ebfb4e60e05ea162da6a3845817aa96f6904d67146a.png)\n\n- Finally, reflect the result across the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=-f(-2x).$\n\n![](images/6f/6f16d9eed1ed1b5fa41c46124f775238ecb759d79261cc66073c1fb304deb468.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554543 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157319 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "947c8ce4-53c5-5765-ab74-62daf58e53e1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Graph Transformations Resulting From Reflections With Shifting"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18e3e3c2-5496-53cf-8c02-e876d2a94f5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/70/70e457825fa6e02a5fc12fda65a38e79df6dcf580baf82f374f530b72963ff15.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553915} {:answer/id #uuid "3a17fc34-f3a5-52e2-abe9-26bde3624def" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4b/4b6237e4e0e151c82d440458720d0e9aa2343bb44b529600d0130ba063b99ca5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553972} {:answer/id #uuid "6fad0e56-8403