of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches and reflections, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo plot $y=f(-x)+2,$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Reflect it across the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=f(-x).$\n\n![](images/1b/1b60eeb882c85423bb0550c2b6def0d073d53747479bf322976db313ffdf4109.png)\n\n \n\n- Then, translate the result  up by $2$ units to get the graph of $y=f(-x)+2.$\n\n![](images/58/58a681bf9aa47521b30761e904dad8e816e2077387c28b132d2480bb39ea4baa.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554539 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157319 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "947c8ce4-53c5-5765-ab74-62daf58e53e1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Graph Transformations Resulting From Reflections With Shifting"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75123df3-af0c-5326-b6f0-9b5d2c22d9d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d6/d64709985bf84c411cce9d99c375cdfc6a81db58f8096c1e23be4fbbb37f8cdb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554105} {:answer/id #uuid "8db3dfee-3c44-5016-97ff-b3ac6e0829e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/54/54dd2266860cfb63305f51c619efa1668b63648864734149db944f9bc99d918c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554169} {:answer/id #uuid "9b682db4-c5bc-55ad-815f-35e7b603f519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/59/5965dff24b2e580ff2da7abbdd979fb3d115cca22a43f8a4967e4b52e3c3af71.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554209} {:answer/id #uuid "b71d69d2-b2d2-552c-8115-33bbaa83b60c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5b/5b22220a4cbf56ee3d66fffae33296839fa5fbf4f29007f56af21ff1cb9f3931.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554269} {:answer/id #uuid "ee93e1f6-2578-53aa-9de8-61504b1abcb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/v